# Incremental agent edits (QA gate)

## One change per agent turn

- Request **one file** or **one test case** per agent session unless the user explicitly approves a batch.
- Good: “Add empty Invoice Number case to `FieldValidation_CovoroTemplate_Test.spec.ts`.”
- Bad: “Fix delivery tests and update all page objects.”

## No refactor-while-fixing

- Fix the stated failure or add the stated case only.
- Do not rename helpers, move layers, or “clean up” unrelated files in the same diff.
- If a fix truly needs a second file (spec + page object), say so first; limit to those two paths.

## Mandatory diff review (team standard)

- **Never accept multi-file agent edits without manual diff review.**
- Before merge: read every changed hunk in Cursor diff or `git diff`; reject drive-by edits.
- Prefer: author test → commit → push → **Cursor PR / code review on diff** → human sign-off → merge.

## Agent behavior

- Propose the smallest diff that satisfies the prompt.
- List files to touch **before** editing; stop after the agreed set.
- Do not read or modify paths outside the scoped task (see `agent-token-scope`).
